{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Woe to those who add house to house.</b> הוי is like a cry of proclamation, or like אוי. The meaning is those who move the boundaries of houses and fields." "<b>Until no place remains.</b> Until there is no place, and the meaning is that they took everything." "<b>And you shall be caused to dwell.</b> From a binyan whose verbal noun is not called by name, among verbs with yod [as third root letter], and likewise והורד המשכן (Numbers 10:17)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:10.970228329Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}